      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": { "level": 2 },
        "content": [{ "type": "text", "text": "Centre rose" }]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [{ "type": "text", "text": "Work a 5-petal rose as in the Irish crochet flower motif pattern. After the last outer petal, do not fasten off." }]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": { "level": 2 },
        "content": [{ "type": "text", "text": "Chain loop rounds" }]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [{ "type": "text", "text": "Round 1: work chain 5 loops around the outer edge of the rose, joining each to a picot. Round 2: work 2 dc into each loop, chain 3 at each corner to begin the square shape. Rounds 3 to 4: continue working dc into the spaces, with chain 5 corner loops at each corner. By round 4 the motif should measure 8 cm square." }]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": { "level": 2 },
        "content": [{ "type": "text", "text": "Finishing" }]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [{ "type": "text", "text": "Fasten off and weave in the ends with the tapestry needle. Block to shape if needed." }]
      }
    ]
